                  "Conduct manual selection of observations",
                  "Filter observations by selection criteria",
                  "Apply data preproccesing"
                ]
              },
              "Description": "The operation that analyzes observational datasets to establish historical trends and variability.",
              "@type": "top:Operation",
              "Label": "Conduct observation analysis",
              "@id": "ops:ConductObservationAnalysis",
              "InformationRoles": [
                {
                  "@type": "top:InformationRole",
                  "@id": "ops:ConductObservationAnalysis/associated-data",
                  "ExpectedType": {
                    "@id": "top:Method",
                    "@type": "owl:Class"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Input": "Calculated indices, slice statistic, change statistic",
              "Output": "Aggregated indices",
              "WorkflowInfo": {
                "Roles": [
                  "CaseSolver"
                ],
                "InformationType": "Optional",
                "BackwardDependencies": [
                  "Compute climate indices"
                ]
              },
              "Description": "The operation that aggregates calculated indices.",
              "@type": "top:Operation",
              "Label": "Conduct spatial aggregation",
              "@id": "ops:ConductSpatialAggregation",
              "InformationRoles": [
                {
                  "@type": "top:InformationRole",
                  "@id": "ops:ConductSpatialAggregation/associated-data",
                  "ExpectedType": {
                    "@id": "top:Method",
                    "@type": "owl:Class"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "Input": "Calculated or aggregated indices, slice or change statistic, or processed climate data, or observation analysis",
              "Output": "Model performance metric",
              "Comment": "We require case solver to add at least some type of quality evaluation metric - regardless it is used to make the final decision or not.",
              "WorkflowInfo": {
                "Roles": [
                  "CaseSolver"
                ],
                "InformationType": "Conditional",
                "Condition": "Obligatory unless case solver decides to only use impact models (like ISIMIP) without input data from climate simulations",
                "BackwardDependencies": [
                  "Filter climate simulations by selection criteria",
                  "Conduct manual selection of climate simulations",
                  "Apply pattern scaling",
                  "Apply additional spatial and/or temporal downscaling",
                  "Filter observations by selection criteria",
                  "Conduct manual selection of observations",
                  "Apply data preproccesing",
                  "Compute climate indices",
                  "Conduct observation analysis",
                  "Conduct spatial aggregation"
                ],
                "ForwardDependencies": [
                  "Select climate simulations"
                ]
              },
              "Description": "The operation that evaluates the performance of climate simulations against observations, by comparing how well climate models reproduce historical climate conditions for selected indices or variables. This evaluation helps determine which models could be more reliable for projecting future climate changes.",
              "@type": "top:Operation",
              "Label": "Evaluate climate simulations",
              "@id": "ops:EvaluateClimateSimulations",
              "InformationRoles": [
                {
                  "@type": "top:InformationRole",
                  "@id": "ops:EvaluateClimateSimulations/associated-data",
                  "ExpectedType": {
                    "@id": "top:Method",
                    "@type": "owl:Class"
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
